WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.443 --> 00:00:07.013
- Fresh Prince asking "I
hear story telling a lot

00:00:07.013 --> 00:00:09.585
nowadays" we talked about this at the top,

00:00:09.585 --> 00:00:11.954
"What's one way I can
do that on social media,

00:00:11.954 --> 00:00:14.871
on Instagram as an example?"

00:00:14.871 --> 00:00:16.885
- I think it's a great
question Fresh Prince,

00:00:16.885 --> 00:00:18.115
and there's a couple of things.

00:00:18.115 --> 00:00:21.474
I think on social, yeah
Instagram is great,

00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:24.195
awesome channel, go
where your audience is.

00:00:24.195 --> 00:00:25.893
If that's the demographics
of your audience

00:00:25.893 --> 00:00:28.375
and they're likely interested
in your idea or product

00:00:28.375 --> 00:00:29.928
then that's absolutely where you go.

00:00:29.928 --> 00:00:33.063
Or Facebook or maybe
more traditional channels

00:00:33.063 --> 00:00:36.350
of Twitter, but I think
definitely it's fantastic,

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:38.091
so you could embrace that channel.

00:00:38.091 --> 00:00:42.394
The other thing, you have
to have compelling content.

00:00:42.394 --> 00:00:46.559
So on things like Instagram,
great visualization,

00:00:46.559 --> 00:00:51.144
pictures, video and also
on social media as well,

00:00:51.144 --> 00:00:54.062
the great thing about
social media is it's not

00:00:54.062 --> 00:00:56.522
one shot, it's a continuous conversation.

00:00:56.522 --> 00:00:58.311
It's a storyteller.

00:00:58.311 --> 00:01:01.753
One of the most compelling
ways to tell your story

00:01:01.753 --> 00:01:03.683
and I guess it's the way you start with,

00:01:03.683 --> 00:01:07.900
is what problem am I
solving for my customer.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:10.860
What is the pain point
that my customer is going

00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:14.610
through everyday that
I'm going to alleviate?

00:01:15.483 --> 00:01:17.739
What is the gain they're
going to get from it?

00:01:17.739 --> 00:01:20.730
If you answer that question,
you're really clear

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.559
about what problem I'm
solving for my customer,

00:01:23.559 --> 00:01:25.794
what is the pain point, and then you show

00:01:25.794 --> 00:01:29.086
through stories, especially with pictures

00:01:29.086 --> 00:01:33.585
and visualization, then I
think you're off to a winner.

00:01:33.585 --> 00:01:35.975
Then, the great thing
with social is you can get

00:01:35.975 --> 00:01:38.188
other people involved and
you can build a community

00:01:38.188 --> 00:01:41.765
where you are one of the opinion leaders

00:01:41.765 --> 00:01:45.444
on the conversation and
you're one of the participants

00:01:45.444 --> 00:01:47.694
in terms of shaping the conversation

00:01:47.694 --> 00:01:49.645
and that's so powerful.

00:01:49.645 --> 00:01:53.997
The first thing is again,
you want to, if you

00:01:53.997 --> 00:01:55.726
got the idea, you know
what you want to do,

00:01:55.726 --> 00:01:58.012
you know what pain
point it solves, you got

00:01:58.012 --> 00:02:01.473
a great idea in terms of
how to show your product

00:02:01.473 --> 00:02:04.535
and you can show it
through demos, pictures,

00:02:04.535 --> 00:02:06.414
videos all that sort of stuff.

00:02:06.414 --> 00:02:08.969
Then, you'd get out
there and do it because

00:02:08.969 --> 00:02:10.144
you'll find other people
out there who will be

00:02:10.144 --> 00:02:12.769
really willing to contribute.

00:02:12.769 --> 00:02:15.587
The great thing is, you
can get loads of almost

00:02:15.587 --> 00:02:17.916
instant feedback, market
research, whatever

00:02:17.916 --> 00:02:20.237
you want to call it, and it's all free.

00:02:20.237 --> 00:02:23.286
It's all free, you just lap it up.

00:02:23.286 --> 00:02:25.745
Evolve your product
according to the advice

00:02:25.745 --> 00:02:30.085
you're getting from the
folks out in the community.

00:02:30.085 --> 00:02:32.196
- I think for any kind
of story telling it's

00:02:32.196 --> 00:02:34.206
understanding first,
what do you stand for,

00:02:34.206 --> 00:02:35.968
what's your mission, what's your value.

00:02:35.968 --> 00:02:38.275
For me, Believe, I want
to help entrepreneurs.

00:02:38.275 --> 00:02:41.673
Everything that I create oozes Believe.

00:02:41.673 --> 00:02:43.973
Every video I make, every interview I do.

00:02:43.973 --> 00:02:45.698
Every picture that I post.

00:02:45.698 --> 00:02:47.289
I think what you want to
do is create something

00:02:47.289 --> 00:02:50.373
that you want to go and
show your grandkids.

00:02:50.373 --> 00:02:52.693
You want to create something
that you're so proud of

00:02:52.693 --> 00:02:54.574
that you want your
grandkids to see in every

00:02:54.574 --> 00:02:57.195
post that you're creating.

00:02:57.195 --> 00:03:01.375
With an Instagram structure,
Instagram typically

00:03:01.375 --> 00:03:05.428
has been, you put your
best picture out there.

00:03:05.428 --> 00:03:08.950
You curate all of these
pictures, you take 1000 pictures

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:11.276
and one of them, your best one is the one

00:03:11.276 --> 00:03:12.569
you're going to put up.

00:03:12.569 --> 00:03:14.378
But the recent change with
stories has been super

00:03:14.378 --> 00:03:17.280
interesting and now you have
the ability to tell stories

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.437
along your day, just like snap chat does,

00:03:20.437 --> 00:03:22.236
it disappears in 24 hours.

00:03:22.236 --> 00:03:25.357
It's a chance to develop
the more human side

00:03:25.357 --> 00:03:27.626
of what you're all about, what
you're routine looks like,

00:03:27.626 --> 00:03:29.497
the behind the scenes,
talking to customers

00:03:29.497 --> 00:03:32.503
and so, it's a great way,
I think that entrepreneurs

00:03:32.503 --> 00:03:35.965
can win because that's how you beat bigger

00:03:35.965 --> 00:03:38.845
players in your industry,
is the human connection.

00:03:38.845 --> 00:03:41.726
It's the why, because
you care more about what

00:03:41.726 --> 00:03:45.224
you're doing than some
other big corporation might

00:03:45.224 --> 00:03:48.787
in your space and so going
all in on your story is

00:03:48.787 --> 00:03:50.345
going to be really important and Instagram

00:03:50.345 --> 00:03:51.305
is a great way to do it.

00:03:51.305 --> 00:03:53.247
These quick, ten second
clips of what's happening

00:03:53.247 --> 00:03:55.570
in your day, why you
started this thing and why

00:03:55.570 --> 00:03:57.005
it's also great is you
don't need to have a big

00:03:57.005 --> 00:04:00.655
budget, Stephen talked
about ti being free.

00:04:00.655 --> 00:04:02.879
People don't expect, with
youtube, there's still

00:04:02.879 --> 00:04:05.910
some expectations over video quality,

00:04:05.910 --> 00:04:08.175
and a lot of players are
spending a lot of money

00:04:08.175 --> 00:04:10.684
with production crews
and camera men and lights

00:04:10.684 --> 00:04:14.292
and all that, and with an Instagram story

00:04:14.292 --> 00:04:17.965
or SnapChat it's expected
to be real, it's expected

00:04:17.965 --> 00:04:20.656
to be a little more
gritty because it's just

00:04:20.656 --> 00:04:22.853
taken from your phone,
and so that's really

00:04:22.853 --> 00:04:25.226
an awesome chance for you to practice

00:04:25.226 --> 00:04:28.022
telling your story, sharing
what is so important

00:04:28.022 --> 00:04:30.308
to you in your day to
day life and a chance

00:04:30.308 --> 00:04:31.509
for your customers and
your audience and your

00:04:31.509 --> 00:04:33.536
followers to understand
you better and connect

00:04:33.536 --> 00:04:35.133
with what you're all about.

00:04:35.133 --> 00:04:38.543
So I would highly recommend
that as a practice,

00:04:38.543 --> 00:04:40.191
even just for you to
practice because you know

00:04:40.191 --> 00:04:41.575
it's going away in 24 hours.

00:04:41.575 --> 00:04:43.492
The thing only lives for
24 hours, those stories,

00:04:43.492 --> 00:04:45.930
so developing the communication skill

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.963
to talk to an audience
is a really valuable

00:04:48.963 --> 00:04:50.963
exercise to go through.

